From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Attard <sattard@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:58:22 -0700
Subject: feat: let the host of a remote NSWindow set more of its behavior

Electron's app shims create their windows through remote_cocoa, where the
host process has no NSWindow to call. This adds what BaseWindow's API
needs and remote_cocoa has no call for:

- NativeWidgetNSWindow.SetMovable, SetClosable and SetMiniaturizable.
- NativeWidgetNSWindow.SetFullscreenable, which decides whether the
  window can go full screen whatever the size constraints say. Without it
  that follows from "resizable and maximizable", which is a different
  question to an app that sets the three separately.
- An empty aspect ratio passed to SetAspectRatio removes the restriction,
  where it used to hit a DCHECK.
- ApplicationHost::set_pid. When the embedder knows the process that hosts
  the application, showing one of its windows yields activation to that
  process and not to whichever running app declares the bundle
  identifier, which the hosted process chooses for itself.

Chromium's own remote windows (PWA shims) call none of these, so there is
nothing here that it needs; the calls could be upstreamed as they are if
it ever does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

